From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:21:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: blur app glass again only when what is behind it
 changed

Each glass window keeps its blurred backdrop for every view and draws it
again until something below it repaints there, the stacking changes or
the window moves. The blur reads only the glass itself, so the redraw
clip no longer grows past it and sets off other glass, and what is
under the rest of the window can be culled. Clones draw their window's
kept backdrop, and windows that aren't painted aren't blurred.

Upstream-Status: luft-only builds on Kestrel's redraw clip filters
---
